Q: why sequelize-cli is not loading config variables? A: <p>If after trying these tips, reach out to me personally, and I will walk you through the process.</p>
<p>I had a heck of time trying to figure this out and I got it working!</p>
<p>You need to rename your config.json to config.js</p>
<p>and ensure that the file contents of the config.js file are now compatible as js code and not json.</p>
<p>Then in your models/index.js file:</p>
<p>on line 9 for const config:     add the .js at the end of config</p>
<pre><code>const config = require(__dirname + &quot;/../config/config&quot;)[env];
</code></pre>
<pre><code>&quot;/../config/config.js&quot;)[env];
</code></pre>
<p>in your package.json file, change the scripts section for start:</p>
<pre><code>&quot;scripts&quot;: {
    &quot;test&quot;: &quot;echo \&quot;Error: no test specified\&quot; &amp;&amp; exit 1&quot;,
    &quot;start&quot;: &quot;nodemon index.js &amp;&amp; node --env-file=.env index.js&quot;
  },

// This bit is optional and not needed if you are not using nodemon for instant automatic page reloads upon saving code:  nodemon index.js &amp;&amp;
</code></pre>
<p>create an .env file in the root of your backend/server folder<br />
create a .gitignore file at the root of your server/backend folder and add .env to it so that github will not post your sensitive .env variables online.</p>
<p>and ensure the names of those variables match what is in the config.js file</p>
<p>For your sequelizerc file, ensure config path is config.js</p>
<pre><code>// .sequelizerc
const path = require('path');

module.exports = {
  'config': path.resolve('config', 'config.js'),
  'models-path': path.resolve('models'),
  'seeders-path': path.resolve('seeders'),
  'migrations-path': path.resolve('migrations')
};
</code></pre>
<p>Hope this helps!!</p>
<p>--Matt</p>
